{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1473265759,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDc4MTE4MjYzNA=="},"added":["enhancement"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1473332650,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0NTU2NDUzMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/763#issuecomment-245564530"},"message":"Just to be sure: Something from git-describe should end up in the aggregated meta data, correct? Just a plain `git describe` call, or maybe we should have a first config option that informs us what parameters are to be used?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1473372077,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0NTc1NTYzNA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/763#issuecomment-245755634"},"message":"On September 8, 2016 7:04:10 AM EDT, Michael Hanke notifications@github.com wrote:\n\n\u003e Just to be sure: Something from git-describe should end up in the\n\u003e aggregated meta data, correct? Just a plain `git describe` call, or\n\u003e maybe we should have a first config option that informs us what\n\u003e parameters are to be used?\n\u003e \n\u003e ## \n\u003e \n\u003e You are receiving this because you authored the thread.\n\u003e Reply to this email directly or view it on GitHub:\n\u003e https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/763#issuecomment-245564530\n\nI think more than that - I would like not to go and edit every dataset meta to specify new version every time it updates - that is done atm via standard git tags mechanism. So I would like to indicate that for specific dataset to use output of git describe as a version. I could of cause adjust crawler to duplicate that information in the tag and in meta, but I don't like duplication","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1474379339,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDc5NTY3MTU4OA=="},"added":["conference agenda item"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1474424058,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0ODQ5MTc5MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/763#issuecomment-248491791"},"message":"@mih may be a compromise could be the output of e.g.\n\n``` shell\n\u003e git describe --match '[v0-9][0-9.]*' --always --long\n2.0.1-0-g7ec9ffd\n```\n\nso yes -- we would enforce some kind of semantic versioning, and if none tag existed:\n\n``` shell\n\u003e git describe --match '[v0-9][0-9.]*' --always --long\nabc7de6\n```\n\nit should become \n\n``` shell\n\u003e echo \"0.0.0-`git log --first-parent --pretty=oneline | wc -l`-g`git describe --match '[v0-9][0-9.]*' --always --long`\"\n0.0.0-29-gabc7de6\n```\n\nthus we would have something depicting order (unlike pure treeish),possibly reflecting upstream's version which we \"capture\" via git tag (after all, all datasets are at least git repositories), but also always with treeish identifier so happen some tag mutates, we could identify the commit.\nSure thing we could also store full treeish in some other field (e.g. `commit` ;-) ), but version itself must be something \"sortable\" to a human eye imho.  FWIW, above form seems also to be digested ok by LooseVersion:\n\n```\n$\u003e python -c 'from distutils.version import LooseVersion as LV, StrictVersion as SV; print LV(\"0.0.0-2-gabcasdf\") \u003e= \"0.0.0-3-asdf\"' \nFalse\n\n$\u003e python -c 'from distutils.version import LooseVersion as LV, StrictVersion as SV; print LV(\"0.0.0-29-gabcasdf\") \u003e= \"0.0.0-3-asdf\"'\nTrue\n```\n\ncollisions (the same # of commits since tag but different state) might happen, but unlikely, and we would be able to catch those and warn if it happens.\n\nAnother (ain't I want to please? ;) ) could be a meld of upstream/semantic and our lovely \"date based\", e.g.  `2.0.1-0-20160909-g7ec9ffd` thus providing immediate feedback on ordering, age, and also uniquely identifying the commit (and still being digestable by git commands directly which react to `-g???????`.  But yeah -- this one is way too long and we have dedicated field for 'modified' anyways.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1474601616,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0OTA5NDI0NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/763#issuecomment-249094245"},"message":"@mih -- your feedback would be appreciated","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1474601686,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0OTA5NDM5NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/763#issuecomment-249094395"},"message":"actually I am getting inclined to not assign any version unless there is a describe based on tag (or from somewhere else), and make a dedicated 'commit' for the 'commit'","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1474652958,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0OTI1ODQ0NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/763#issuecomment-249258444"},"message":"Yes, sounds good: no version without a tag, commit stored in commit. Something like `2.0.1-0-g7ec9ffd` looks good to me.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1475875200,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1MjM2Mzg1MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/763#issuecomment-252363851"},"message":"I guess it is for me to work on @mih?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1520529348,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MTU1NjY0Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/763#issuecomment-371556643"},"message":"In current (codename `meta6` but version indicator `v1`)  version of metadata, the version of the dataset is stored within aggregate_v1.json \n```\n$\u003e grep -A20 ds000001 aggregate_v1.json \n\"openfmri/ds000001\":\n{\n\"content_info\":\n\"objects/87/cn-1d35795a1ba0410f271672d1f11d7c.xz\",\n\"datalad_version\":\n\"0.9.1.dev1\",\n\"dataset_info\":\n\"objects/87/ds-1d35795a1ba0410f271672d1f11d7c\",\n\"extractors\":\n[\n\"datalad_core\",\n\"nifti1\",\n\"xmp\",\n\"bids\"\n],\n\"id\":\n\"233cc486-7d0e-11e6-855b-002590f97d84\",\n\"refcommit\":\n\"ea98f90157459b3e70a7d7768ce1a0a6bf767746\"\n},\n```\nbut still lacks comparable version.  Do you think @mih it would be the right place to add it?  what name (`refdescribe`?)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1520530210,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MTU2MTIwNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/763#issuecomment-371561207"},"message":"we should add this info, but not there. I will push some local changes I have here that introduce a better place, i think","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1520533008,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MTU3NTI3OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/763#issuecomment-371575279"},"message":"but I do not see any other place where it could be added really, since ds-* shouldn't be the one changing with every aggregation if metadata doesn't change.  Where do you see it ?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1520533330,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MTU3Njg0NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/763#issuecomment-371576844"},"message":"Ah, check the diff of aggregate.py in that PR. I record the commit hash of the state of the dataset that we are describing. That commit hash will not change, if we 